  "body": "The current [Device interface](http://webbluetoothcg.github.io/web-bluetooth/#bluetooth-devices) exposes 2-3 unique IDs for the device (`deviceID`, `address`, and possibly `name`), and allows sites to enumerate the Services the device defines, which is probably also enough to fingerprint the device.\n\nHow much of this do we need to expose to let people write useful apps? Does the fact that a user has to explicitly pair each device with the site mitigate the privacy concern?\n",
